{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a70e4141897b0a821","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hw2aZhUYsRE3ZjPxhrVDHh","description":"Writing plans/json-vs-sqlite-notes/plan.md","subagent_type":"plan-smith:plan-writer","usage":{"total_tokens":15481,"tool_uses":3,"duration_ms":42174},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"015bada9-c26d-4ca9-b8e2-b940c04997ab","session_id":"f834d1f0-9940-45ea-a285-664eae2261cb"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfYwzLtx9qmLKLGNcsV7P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lc5XtC98fhz3csPRBbBiWr","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/jx/81xz9_xj7x31h6mwxd7qrlj40000gn/T/ps-n02-9mmtfsy2/plans/json-vs-sqlite-notes/plan.md","content":"# Notes storage: JSON file vs SQLite\n- Frame: backward / Style: opus (standalone)\n- Pick: one JSON file, saved atomically; SQLite on trigger.\n\n## Anchors\nHabit check: my reflex is \"SQLite, it's canonical\"; the frame makes anchors decide.\n- A1 A crash mid-save never corrupts notes. Kills: in-place JSON overwrite.\n- A2 Full save under 100 ms (arbitrary; replace after first measurement). Kills: JSON past ~5,000 notes.\n- A3 No dependency beyond the runtime's standard library. Kills: SQLite where no driver ships.\n\nIntersection: A2 and A3 collide only at scale. A1 roofs both; build it first.\n\n## Assumptions\n- **Under ~5,000 notes / 5 MB.** If wrong: SQLite. Check: count after one month.\n- No body search. If wrong: SQLite with full-text search.\n\n## Steps\n1. Shape `{\"version\":1,\"notes\":[{id,title,body,updated}]}`. Independent; serves A1–A3.\n2. Save = write temp file, fsync, rename. Needs 1; verifies A1.\n3. Implementer logs save duration. Needs 2; verifies A2.\n\nOff-anchor: title/body editing ships; search deferred to the trigger below. Unmeasured category: hand-readable backups, which favor JSON.\n\n## Rejected: SQLite\nRevive when notes exceed 5,000, a save exceeds 100 ms, or body search is requested. Hosted DB stays out.\n\n## Done\nThe implementer kill -9s the app during 100 scripted saves of a 1,000-note file; every relaunch parses and shows the pre- or post-save state.\n\n## Frame deviations & habit regressions\n- A3 is weak: most runtimes bundle SQLite, so its kill barely bites.\n- A2 is weakest: 100 ms and 5,000 are arbitrary, not derived.\n- Step 2 is convention, not derived.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2746,"cache_read_input_tokens":9386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2746,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hw2aZhUYsRE3ZjPxhrVDHh","session_id":"f834d1f0-9940-45ea-a285-664eae2261cb","uuid":"bdd2a767-18d1-41fd-a0b3-36ffc8e4c465","timestamp":"2026-09-30T03:55:34.610Z","request_id":"req_011CfYwzLVtMyJzsBP2DYSAB","subagent_type":"plan-smith:plan-writer","task_description":"Write JSON vs SQLite plan"}
