{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015AmZ2BiASfnLo9DmC29RHg","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/var/folders/jx/81xz9_xj7x31h6mwxd7qrlj40000gn/T/ps-n02-9mmtfsy2/plans/json-vs-sqlite-notes/plan.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f834d1f0-9940-45ea-a285-664eae2261cb","uuid":"45f38644-a612-4701-8dec-03dbc73d8179","timestamp":"2026-09-30T03:56:09.095Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/jx/81xz9_xj7x31h6mwxd7qrlj40000gn/T/ps-n02-9mmtfsy2/plans/json-vs-sqlite-notes/plan.md","oldString":"- Step 2 is convention, not derived.","newString":"- Step 2 is convention.","originalFile":"# Notes storage: JSON file vs SQLite\n- Frame: backward / Style: opus\n- Pick: one JSON file, saved atomically; SQLite on trigger.\n\n## Anchors\nHabit check: my reflex is \"SQLite, it's canonical\"; the frame makes anchors decide.\n- A1 A crash mid-save never corrupts notes. Kills: in-place JSON overwrite.\n- A2 Full save under 100 ms (arbitrary; replace after first measurement). Kills: JSON past ~5,000 notes.\n- A3 No dependency beyond the runtime's standard library. Kills: SQLite where no driver ships.\n\nIntersection: A2 and A3 collide only at scale. A1 roofs both; build it first.\n\n## Assumptions\n- **Under ~5,000 notes / 5 MB.** If wrong: SQLite. Check: count after one month.\n- No body search. If wrong: SQLite with full-text search.\n\n## Steps\n1. Shape `{\"version\":1,\"notes\":[{id,title,body,updated}]}`. Independent; serves A1–A3.\n2. Save = write temp file, fsync, rename. Needs 1; verifies A1.\n3. Log save duration. Needs 2; verifies A2.\n\nOff-anchor: title/body editing ships; search deferred to the trigger below. Unmeasured: hand-readable backups favor JSON.\n\n## Rejected: SQLite\nRevive when notes exceed 5,000, a save exceeds 100 ms, or body search is requested. Hosted DB stays out.\n\n## Done\nKill -9 the app during 100 scripted saves of a 1,000-note file; every relaunch parses and shows the pre- or post-save state.\n\n## Frame deviations & habit regressions\n- A3 is weak: most runtimes bundle SQLite, so its kill barely bites.\n- A2 is weakest: 100 ms and 5,000 are arbitrary, not derived.\n- Step 2 is convention, not derived.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":30,"oldLines":4,"newStart":30,"newLines":4,"lines":[" ## Frame deviations & habit regressions"," - A3 is weak: most runtimes bundle SQLite, so its kill barely bites."," - A2 is weakest: 100 ms and 5,000 are arbitrary, not derived.","-- Step 2 is convention, not derived.","+- Step 2 is convention."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
