{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfYx6QuD6FZFPnDJW1AYF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan recommends a single JSON file, saved atomically, and switching to SQLite only if one of the triggers below fires. It is 248 words by `wc -w`. Full text of `plans/json-vs-sqlite-notes/plan.md`:\n\n---\n\n# Notes storage: JSON file vs SQLite\n- Frame: backward / Style: opus\n- Pick: one JSON file, saved atomically; SQLite on trigger.\n\n## Anchors\nHabit check: my reflex is \"SQLite, it's canonical\"; the frame makes anchors decide.\n- A1 A crash mid-save never corrupts notes. Kills: in-place JSON overwrite.\n- A2 Full save under 100 ms (arbitrary; replace after first measurement). Kills: JSON past ~5,000 notes.\n- A3 No dependency beyond the runtime's standard library. Kills: SQLite where no driver ships.\n\nIntersection: A2 and A3 collide only at scale. A1 roofs both; build it first.\n\n## Assumptions\n- **Under ~5,000 notes / 5 MB.** If wrong: SQLite. Check: count after one month.\n- No body search. If wrong: SQLite with full-text search.\n\n## Steps\n1. Shape `{\"version\":1,\"notes\":[{id,title,body,updated}]}`. Independent; serves A1–A3.\n2. Save = write temp file, fsync, rename. Needs 1; verifies A1.\n3. Log save duration. Needs 2; verifies A2.\n\nOff-anchor: title/body editing ships; search deferred to the trigger below. Unmeasured: hand-readable backups favor JSON.\n\n## Rejected: SQLite\nRevive when notes exceed 5,000, a save exceeds 100 ms, or body search is requested. Hosted DB stays out.\n\n## Done\nKill -9 the app during 100 scripted saves of a 1,000-note file; every relaunch parses and shows the pre- or post-save state.\n\n## Frame deviations & habit regressions\n- A3 is weak: most runtimes bundle SQLite, so its kill barely bites.\n- A2 is weakest: 100 ms and 5,000 are arbitrary, not derived.\n- Step 2 is convention.\n\n---\n\n**How it was made:**\n- **Length fix:** the writer's draft came to 256 words by `wc -w`. I cut wording only, with no change to any decision, to get it to 248.\n- **Skipped steps:** I skipped the confirmation question as you asked. I also skipped the wiring audit, which only runs for build-out plans, not decision plans.\n- **Model record:** the writer ran on the `opus` alias. The run didn't report an exact model id, so the packet lists it as unknown.\n- **Weak spot:** the \"no extra dependency\" criterion (A3) is weak, as the plan itself admits. If your runtime already includes SQLite, it no longer rules SQLite out, and the choice rests only on the note-count and no-search assumptions.\n\nNo code was written and nothing was committed. The context packet is at `plans/json-vs-sqlite-notes/packet.md`. Tell me whether you adopt, edit or reject the plan, and I'll add that to the packet's Retrospective section."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":907,"cache_read_input_tokens":74923,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":907},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f834d1f0-9940-45ea-a285-664eae2261cb","uuid":"34e8af9a-3009-4c64-a3a7-5375b20a0928","timestamp":"2026-09-30T03:56:29.197Z","request_id":"req_011CfYx6QRwfhheCGBrQu5wp"}
